      "comment": "Checked the five research_append calls in the run, not the rationale. The recorded rationale misdescribes the failure: the rejections were not subject_person_id / objective_type / numeric priority. They were a missing-required-fields rejection on questions[0] (selection_basis, depends_on, unblocks, resolved, resolution_assertion_ids), then TWO consecutive invalid selection_basis values -- 'pedigree_gap', then 'missing_ancestor'. research_append returned a worked example with each rejection, so the valid shape was in hand before the second and third guesses. Keeping 2: three round-trips to land one entry, with the answer supplied each time, is an argument defect rather than a guardrail working normally. If this recurs the durable fix is the tool description listing selection_basis's valid values, not skill prose."
