      "comment": "Raising to 3. The dock was for a person_quality call returning fixture_not_found. Checked the test definition and the fixture corpus: this test declares exactly one fixture (person-read-moreau-person-level-sources) and there is no person-quality fixture for MRQ1-JBM, while sibling init-project tests do declare them (person-quality-clean-BRNN-MOM, -MRCR-CH1). The call itself was well-formed -- person_quality({personId: 'MRQ1-JBM', detail: true}), matched kind 'none' -- and the harness's own response tells the CALLER to declare a fixture. That is an eval-fixture gap, not a wrong argument, and scoring it down teaches the skill to avoid a tool that works in production."
    },
