      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Agreeing with 2. The reply claims Jean Baptiste's death 'has no source attached to it at all' and lists it as Finding 1, when the person_read response carried three sources for him. That is a factual claim about the data in hand that the data contradicts, and it is the kind of error a researcher would act on. The rest -- all four family members with accurate names, dates, places and relationships -- is why this is not a 1."
